Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:41:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 111/154] fix(split): route a cmd+option link click into the
 atrium split
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A link click with cmd+option asks for NEW_SPLIT_VIEW. Stock handling pairs
the new tab through TabStripModel::AddToNewSplit, which an Atrium window
never populates, so the second pane silently never appeared. Browser::
OpenURLFromTab now hands that disposition to OpenLinkInAtriumSplit, and the
hover card names the chord again.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
index b7b01080ce2ef..4982efcff8008 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
@@ -292,6 +292,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_feature_check.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_peek_intercept.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/atrium/atrium_status_bubble_hook.h"
 #include "ui/display/display.h"
@@ -1516,6 +1517,24 @@ WebContents* Browser::OpenURLFromTab(
   }
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
+  // Cmd+Option on a link is NEW_SPLIT_VIEW, whose stock handling pairs the new
+  // tab through TabStripModel::AddToNewSplit - a path Atrium's TabStripModel
+  // never populates, so the pane silently never appears. NEW_BACKGROUND_TAB
+  // because OpenLinkInAtriumSplit opens the link itself and would recurse.
+  if (params.disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_SPLIT_VIEW && source &&
+      atrium::IsAtriumBrowserWindowEnabled()) {
+    OpenURLParams split_params(params);
+    split_params.disposition = WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_BACKGROUND_TAB;
+    if (atrium::OpenLinkInAtriumSplit(this, source, split_params,
+                                      /*stacked=*/false)) {
+      return source;  // No new WebContents created on this path.
+    }
+    // Nothing Atrium can split - a devtools or popup window, say - so open a
+    // plain tab rather than fall into a split this window cannot build.
+    return OpenURLFromTab(source, split_params,
+                          std::move(navigation_handle_callback));
+  }
+
   // Peek mode (2026-07-10 plan, Q1): shift+click on Mac maps to
   // NEW_WINDOW (ui/base/window_open_disposition_utils.cc's
   // DispositionFromClick) - intercept it here, before a real window/tab is
